<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<metadata>

  <!--
    Java-binding transforms for the vendored org.libsdl.app sources.

    THE PROBLEM
    ===========
    Java allows several top-level classes per file, but only one may be public.
    SDLActivity.java and SDLControllerManager.java each declare public classes plus
    several package-private helpers (SDLClipboardHandler, SDLGenericMotionListener_API14,
    SDLHapticHandler, SDLJoystickHandler).

    The binding generator does not emit bindings for package-private types - correctly,
    they are not API - but it DOES emit the protected static fields whose type they are.
    The result is generated C# that references types it never generated:

        error CS0234: The type or namespace name 'SDLClipboardHandler' does not exist

    THE FIX
    =======
    Remove those four fields from the binding. They are internal plumbing that SDL's own
    Java code uses; nothing on the C# side has any business touching them, and the Java
    fields themselves are untouched - only the C# projection is trimmed.

    The XPaths are not guesswork: the generator writes the exact path for every member
    into the generated source as a comment, and these were copied from there.

    IF SDL IS UPDATED and new package-private helpers appear, this file is where the
    resulting CS0234 is fixed. See java/PROVENANCE.md for the update procedure.
  -->

  <remove-node path="/api/package[@name='org.libsdl.app']/class[@name='SDLActivity']/field[@name='mClipboardHandler']" />
  <remove-node path="/api/package[@name='org.libsdl.app']/class[@name='SDLActivity']/field[@name='mMotionListener']" />
  <remove-node path="/api/package[@name='org.libsdl.app']/class[@name='SDLControllerManager']/field[@name='mHapticHandler']" />
  <remove-node path="/api/package[@name='org.libsdl.app']/class[@name='SDLControllerManager']/field[@name='mJoystickHandler']" />

</metadata>
